title: DeadLock Ransomware Encrypted File and Ransom Note Artifacts
id: 0ad67621-8d62-4f84-9824-fdfabea69c2a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects file artifacts documented for DeadLock ransomware (Microsoft
    Threat Intelligence, Aug 2026): files renamed with the .dlock extension,
    text ransom notes named HOW_RECOVER.<UID>.txt dropped per encrypted
    directory, and the self-contained HTML recovery chat
    RECOVERY_CHAT.<UID>.html dropped to drive roots and Desktop folders.
references:
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/08/10/deadlock-ransomware-breaking-down-a-rust-based-encryptor-with-decentralized-recovery-infrastructure/
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/deadlock-ransomware-uses-blockchain-to-resist-infrastructure-takedown/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/13
tags:
    - attack.t1486
    - attack.t1490
    - attack.t1070
logsource:
    category: file_event
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_dlock:
        TargetFilename|endswith: '.dlock'
    selection_note_txt:
        TargetFilename|contains: 'HOW_RECOVER.'
        TargetFilename|endswith: '.txt'
    selection_note_html:
        TargetFilename|contains: 'RECOVERY_CHAT.'
        TargetFilename|endswith: '.html'
    condition: selection_dlock or selection_note_txt or selection_note_html
falsepositives:
    - Files legitimately using a .dlock extension outside this campaign (rare); corroborate with encryption behavior and ransom notes
    - Development or decoy files named HOW_RECOVER/RECOVERY_CHAT; validate against adjacent encryption activity
level: high
---
title: DeadLock Ransomware Leak Site Network Connections
id: a52e6fef-dffc-4807-a0f6-251ae44a95a4
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects network connections to DeadLock ransomware leak-site domains
    published as indicators of compromise by Microsoft Threat Intelligence:
    deadlock.liveblog365.com, dlock.liveblog365.com,
    deadlockblog.great-site.net and deadlockblog.medianewsonline.com,
    plus the .onion mirror deadblogdbdu5wprek7wa2o4ce7rnt6u6ntqeud3hzjjcveosgpsqqqd.
references:
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/08/10/deadlock-ransomware-breaking-down-a-rust-based-encryptor-with-decentralized-recovery-infrastructure/
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/deadlock-ransomware-uses-blockchain-to-resist-infrastructure-takedown/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/13
tags:
    - attack.t1486
    - attack.t1562
    - attack.t1070
logsource:
    category: network_connection
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_domains:
        DestinationHostname|endswith:
            - 'deadlock.liveblog365.com'
            - 'dlock.liveblog365.com'
            - 'deadlockblog.great-site.net'
            - 'deadlockblog.medianewsonline.com'
    selection_onion:
        DestinationHostname|contains: 'deadblogdbdu5wprek7wa2o4ce7rnt6u6ntqeud3hzjjcveosgpsqqqd'
    condition: 1 of selection_*
falsepositives:
    - None known; these domains are unique to the DeadLock leak-site infrastructure and are not legitimate services
level: high
